From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 15:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: BCM5301X: R6400: add the USB LED trigger sources

The USB LEDs have no trigger-sources, so the usbport trigger warns once
for every USB port when it starts:

  leds white:usb-1: Failed to get trigger sources for /leds/led-usb1

Name the ports as the other BCM5301X boards do (USB 1: OHCI, EHCI and
XHCI port 1; USB 2: OHCI and EHCI port 2) and make usbport the default
trigger. The R6400 v2 includes this file, so it covers both versions.

Tested on the R6400 v1 and v2: the warning is gone, and a USB stick
lights USB 1 in the front port (USB 3.0) and USB 2 in the back port.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Erik Conijn <egc112@msn.com>
---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4708-netgear-r6400-v1.dts
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/broadcom/bcm4708-netgear-r6400-v1.dts
@@ -95,6 +95,9 @@
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_USB;
 			function-enumerator = <1>;
 			gpios = <&chipcommon 12 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			trigger-sources = <&ohci_port1>, <&ehci_port1>,
+					  <&xhci_port1>;
+			linux,default-trigger = "usbport";
 		};
 
 		led-usb2 {
@@ -102,6 +105,8 @@
 			function = LED_FUNCTION_USB;
 			function-enumerator = <2>;
 			gpios = <&chipcommon 13 GPIO_ACTIVE_LOW>;
+			trigger-sources = <&ohci_port2>, <&ehci_port2>;
+			linux,default-trigger = "usbport";
 		};
 	};
 
